				"Gradient descent as landscape navigation",
				"Clustering as unsupervised pattern finding",
				"Neural networks as layered feature extraction",
				"Generative models as learned distributions",
				"The gap between model and reality"
			],
			"content": [
				"ML_Evolution: Carl Sims creatures + evolving flowers \u00e2\u20ac\u201d selection pressure shapes form without explicit design",
				"ML_Gradient_Landscape: Gradient descent visualization + PCA \u00e2\u20ac\u201d navigating loss surfaces, seeing high dimensions",
				"ML_Classification: K-means clustering + SVM + random forest \u00e2\u20ac\u201d different ways to draw boundaries in data",
				"ML_Neural_Networks: Neural network visualization + architecture exploration \u00e2\u20ac\u201d layers learn features",
				"ML_Perception: Computer vision + CNNs + attention \u00e2\u20ac\u201d how machines learn to see",
				"ML_Sequence_Memory: LSTMs + transformers \u00e2\u20ac\u201d learning temporal patterns and long-range dependencies",
				"ML_Generative: GANs + VAEs \u00e2\u20ac\u201d machines that generate, not just classify",
